  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nIssued 205 PM MDT SAT OCT 3 2026\nThe upper-level ridge will rebuild over the region Tuesday and \nstick around through at least Thursday. This will keep \ntemperatures well above normal, averaging 10 to 20 degrees above\nnormal through the week and within a few degrees of record \nhighs in many locations. Additionally with this pattern, clear \nskies, dry conditions, and weak winds are expected. \n\nAn upper level trough will approach the Pacific Northwest on \nFriday and move inland over the weekend. Significant differences\nin the timing and strength of the trough exist between the \nensembles, but cluster analysis is converging on the trough \nmoving overhead at some point during the weekend. With this \npattern, cooler temperatures are expected over the weekend, with\nlower confidence on precipitation location and timing. \nAdditionally, winds will become breezy Friday and Saturday, \nespecially over higher terrain.",
